 of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids in Johnson County has come in under 90% of normal in January to February 38 years of the 75 on record since 1951. In 2025 that middle ran 50% of normal in August to September and 60% in September to October. Grid 22646 had its driest year in 1956 at 55% of normal. For 2026, a preliminary estimate on grid 22645 puts July to August at 89.5.</p>"}
